CICD integrationwith Helm 

1. Developer pushes code

Git repository

2. Jenkins builds and tests

Run tests, build the container image

3. Push image to registry

For example, AWS ECR

4. Validate Helm chart

Lint and render manifests

5. Deploy to Kubernetes

Helm upgrade and rollout verification

Example Jenkins pipeline
pipeline {
    agent any

    environment {
        RELEASE = 'web-prod'
        NAMESPACE = 'prod'
        CHART = './helm/web-app'
    }

    stages {
        stage('Checkout') {
            steps {
                checkout scm
            }
        }

        stage('Validate Helm') {
            steps {
                sh 'helm lint $CHART'
                sh 'helm template $RELEASE $CHART -n $NAMESPACE'
            }
        }

        stage('Build and Push Image') {
            steps {
                echo 'Build, tag and push the image to ECR'
            }
        }

        stage('Deploy') {
            steps {
                sh '''
                  helm upgrade --install $RELEASE $CHART \
                    --namespace $NAMESPACE \
                    --create-namespace \
                    --wait \
                    --timeout 5m
                '''
            }
        }

        stage('Verify Deployment') {
            steps {
                sh '''
                  kubectl rollout status deployment/<deployment-name> \
                    -n $NAMESPACE --timeout=5m
                '''
            }
        }
    }
}

